# FreeBSD ports files of lang/php84 that are NOT applied, with the reason.
# Format: "<port file>: <reason>"; listed in the branch README and in the release notes.
# Documentation only: editing this file does not rebuild the branch.
patch-configure.ac: ports build layout: split packaging (ext/php_config.h include, no pthreads check) and the ports' PEAR include_path; the upstream defaults of a hand build are kept
patch-ext_hash_xxhash_xxhash.h: PowerPC VSX (AltiVec) and s390x only; no effect on amd64
patch-ext_pcre_php__pcre.h: only affects `--with-external-pcre` builds (`#include "pcre2.h"` becomes `<pcre2.h>`); the bundled PCRE and the upstream include work as is
libressl-patch-ext_openssl_openssl.c: only for builds against LibreSSL (the port applies it only then)
php_session.h: ports split packaging: a header the port copies into ext/session to build ext/soap as a separate package
php_fpm.in: the rc.d script of the port, not a source patch; your own rc.d scripts stay in use
